# CODEOWNERS for BettaPay-Contract
#
# This file defines who must review changes to cross-cutting or
# governance-sensitive paths before they can be merged (ADRs, shared
# protocol constants, deployment/CI scripts, and repo-governance files).
#
# NOTE FOR MAINTAINERS: The handles below are placeholders inferred from
# commit history (most active contributor / merger of PRs into `main`).
# Replace `@0xjhay` with the actual maintainer username(s) and/or create a
# `@Betta-Pay/maintainers` GitHub team and reference it here once it
# exists, so review load isn't pinned to a single person.
#
# Syntax reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# - Last matching pattern wins, so more specific rules are listed after
#   more general ones.
# - Patterns are relative to the repository root and use gitignore-style
#   globbing.

# Default fallback: unmatched paths have no required owner.

# Architecture Decision Records — decisions here affect both contracts and
# must stay consistent with the code that implements them.
/adr/                              @0xjhay

# Shared protocol constants — used by both governance_contract and
# settlement_contract; drift here silently changes fee/TTL/recovery
# behavior across the whole protocol.
bettapay_common/src/constants.rs   @0xjhay
**/constants.rs                    @0xjhay

# Deployment / simulation / CI-support scripts.
/scripts/                          @0xjhay
/Makefile                          @0xjhay

# Repo governance and process files.
/CODEOWNERS                        @0xjhay
/SECURITY.md                       @0xjhay
/CONTRIBUTING.md                   @0xjhay
/.github/workflows/                @0xjhay
